    "lawCode": "Amd §352.3, Fam Ct Act",
    "lawSection": "Family Court Act",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5421\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the family court act, in relation to the issuance of\norders of protection for the benefit of witnesses\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nTo authorize family courts to issue orders of protection for the\nprotection of witnesses.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nAmends § 352.3 of the family court act adding provisions to require a\ndefendant to stay away from any witness designated by the court.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nWitnesses called to testify in family court are not afforded any legal\nprotection. Very often witnesses are reluctant to testify out of fear.\nProviding for a court order of protection for certain witnesses will\nfacilitate their willingness to come forward and testify even when\nthey feel their testimony may endanger their safety. While an order of\nprotection cannot guarantee the safety of a witness, it can help.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nNinetieth day after it becomes law.\n",
